# CH14 — Roads Grow Teeth. Flooded Rootward: Elowen's survivors, three crossings, the Ash-Tide Warden (B11).

@scene CH14_CAMP once
say narr | A camp on the high roots. Tarps, a cook fire, and forty people who have been waiting for the water to decide something.
say nera | Raven? Aurex. You're alive. Good. Don't touch the map.
say dain | Hello to you too.
say nera | There are three crossings north of here. Two of them drown people. One doesn't. I know which. So I lead every group across myself.
say oriel | How many trips a day?
say nera | As many as it takes.
say mara | Which is why half of them are still here after two weeks. Nobody can wait for one guide forever, Elowen.
say nera | If I hand out the map and somebody takes the wrong crossing -
say mara | Then we make every crossing the right one.
say nera | ...The current's being pushed south by something in the old sluice. If the sluice lets go, the water drops. The walkways can be raised with the levers - if you know which way they lift.
objective oriel | Raise all three walkways in the Three Crossings (north), then find what is diverting the current.
@end

@scene CH14_NERA_CAMP
if event:CH14_CAMP after
say nera | Who's that? Oh - it's you.
end
label after
say nera | Three levers, three walkways. Up is up - don't overthink it. The thing in the sluice is another story.
@end

@scene CH14_MARA
say mara | She's been carrying the whole camp on one map. Let's give her arms a rest.
@end

@scene CH14_CHILD
say child | Elowen says the forest used to be dry. I don't believe her. Trees can't live without swimming.
@end

@scene CH14_ELDER
say elder | My hip won't take the ford twice. I'll go once, on a proper walkway, or not at all.
@end

@scene CH14_ROUTE1
if flag:d03p_route1 done
sfx FX010
set d03p_route1
say narr | The west lever lifts. A walkway rises dripping out of the flood, planks still marked with old guild paint.
call CH14_ROUTES
end
label done
say narr | The west walkway is raised.
@end

@scene CH14_ROUTE2
if flag:d03p_route2 done
sfx FX010
set d03p_route2
say narr | The middle lever groans. The centre walkway surfaces, green with weed.
call CH14_ROUTES
end
label done
say narr | The middle walkway is raised.
@end

@scene CH14_ROUTE3
if flag:d03p_route3 done
sfx FX010
set d03p_route3
say narr | The east lever snaps up. The last walkway rises, and for a moment the whole pool is quiet.
call CH14_ROUTES
end
label done
say narr | The east walkway is raised.
@end

@scene CH14_ROUTES
if flag:d03p_route1,flag:d03p_route2,flag:d03p_route3 all
say narr | (The current still tugs at the lowered crossings.)
end
label all
objective oriel | All three crossings are up. Follow the current north to the old sluice.
@end

@scene CH14_WARDEN once
music silence
say narr | The old sluice. A shape of bark and silt and drowned iron is holding the gate shut with its whole body, forcing the river south over the camp.
say oriel | It thinks it's holding back the flood. It is the flood.
say narr | The Warden turns. Water surges toward the front row.
battle B11 noflee
set b11_done
music M021
say narr | The Warden sinks, and the sluice gate swings free. The water level drops a hand's width, then another.
xp 900
@end

@scene CH14_NERA once
show nera_s 17 16 up C05
say nera | You did it. The current's falling.
say mara | Now the map.
say nera | ...There's only one. It took me four years.
say mara | Then it's the most valuable thing in the camp, and it belongs to the camp.
say nera | If someone reads it wrong -
say oriel | Then they ask someone who read it right. That is how maps work when more than one person owns them.
wait 0.5
say nera | Fine. We make copies. One per family. Warnings in the margins. Names of who keeps each crossing.
say nera | It's a start. Not a finish. I'm not done paying for what I sold, back before any of this.
say dain | Come with us?
say nera | Someone's got to find Morwen. She never could read a map.
hide nera_s
join C05
call OV_INFERNA
chapter CH14
set brackenford_routes
objective dain | Brackenford's new crossings are open. Take the repaired ferry from Hearthward east to Bellharbor to find Morwen.
rumor | Hearthward's ferryman has his caulk back. The ferry to the Glass Coast runs again.
level_floor 26
@end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Brackenford (post)
@scene T01P_MARA
if ch:CH20 q01
if ch:CH14 after
say mara | I split my days between here and Hearthward. We count the shelter by name every night - that part I won't hand to anyone.
end
label after
say mara | New crossings, copies of Elowen's map on every door. Brackenford's two halves talk again.
end
label q01
call Q01_HOOK
@end

@scene T01P_SHELTER
say elder | The bunkhouse is a shelter now. Forty cots. The forewoman counts us by name every night. Nobody's a number in here.
@end

@scene T01P_INN
say elder | A cot and a bowl. Nobody's charged.
inn 0
@end

@scene T01P_DEPOT
say baker | The bakery's a footbridge depot. Bread in the morning, planks in the afternoon, and I still burn the rye.
shop SHOP_T01
@end

@scene T01P_CAMP_WEST
if ch:CH20 q05
say farmer | The west camp wants the road to the mill first. The east camp wants the road to the clinic. We'll see.
end
label q05
call Q05_HOOK
@end

@scene T01P_CAMP_EAST
say worker | Clinic road first. Grain's no good to a man with a fever.
@end

@scene T01P_STOREKEEPER
say keeper | I kept extending credit after the quarry stopped paying. Now there's no quarry and no pay. I'm still extending it. Somebody has to believe in tomorrow.
@end

@scene T01P_SALVAGE
say worker | Salvage crew. Anything we pull out of the sealed ruins goes to Hearthward's salvage chest - with the owner's name, if we can find it.
@end
